{
  "id": "body-distortion",
  "term": "body distortion",
  "definition": "Body distortion is a change in normal body posture or movement pattern that happens when a person compensates for a missing or limited function, such as wrist rotation after upper-limb amputation. In this context, it refers to awkward whole-body adjustments during tasks, which can reduce comfort and may contribute to emotional distress such as anxiety or depression.",
